{
  "configuration_id": "config_004",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: scgpt+resnet50+avgpool+concat → 51.2% acc, 4.33 GPU-hrs), evidence is extremely sparse and we need to reduce uncertainty about which design axis matters most. Config_004 isolates a single variable—changing fusion from concat to weighted—while keeping all other components identical to the baseline. This is the cheapest possible informative experiment (~4.3 GPU-hrs, same architecture as config_001). If weighted fusion improves accuracy, it confirms that learned modality balancing is a productive direction and gives us a cheap building block to stack further improvements (e.g., transformer aggregation, stronger image encoder) on top of. If it does not help, we rule out fusion as a lever and can redirect budget toward higher-impact changes (aggregation, encoders). This single-variable ablation is the best use of experiment 2 because it maximizes information per GPU-hour under high uncertainty, avoids committing to expensive architectural changes (transformer, ViT-L) before we know which axis to exploit, and keeps total cost low (~8.7 GPU-hrs cumulative) leaving ample budget for the 8 remaining experiments."
}

